  "marketSentiment": "NEUTRAL_BULLISH",
  "macroTheme": "NFP June +57K devastates the soft-landing narrative -- US30 ATH on rate-cut rotation while NAS100 prints a bearish reversal on growth-scare. Gold breaks above all identified resistance levels (4,031/4,078/4,130), full BEARISH-to-BULLISH reversal. Warsh at Sintra: inflation too high, no July guidance. GER40 new year high.",
  "macroOverview": "NFP June came in at +57K on Thursday July 2, a severe miss vs +110K consensus. Prior month revised down to +129K from +172K. Unemployment 4.2% (up from 4.1%). The print repriced September 2026 as a live Fed cut meeting. Warsh at ECB Sintra on July 1 was hawkish on inflation but declined to signal July action. ADP June +98K and ISM Manufacturing June 53.3 (employment sub-index 49.7) all pointed to a softening labor and industrial backdrop. Market reaction diverged sharply: US30 surged to a new ATH of 52,903, GER40 printed a new year high of 25,826, gold broke through all resistance to close above 4,187, silver gained 6% on the week, and GBPCAD broke above the prior year high of 1.8915. NAS100 had a whipsaw session -- initial spike to 30,044 on rate-cut hope followed by a crash to 29,087 close at 29,329 on growth-scare selling. All three Wednesday conviction trades were stopped out.",
